+Disabling retries
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+During development and testing you may want to turn retrying off without
+removing the decorator. Pass ``enabled=False`` to :func:`~tenacity.retry`,
+:class:`~tenacity.Retrying` or :class:`~tenacity.AsyncRetrying`. The function
+is then called exactly once, with no retry logic, and any exception it raises
+propagates unchanged.
+
+.. testcode::
+
+    @retry(stop=stop_after_attempt(3), enabled=False)
+    def raise_my_exception_once():
+        raise MyException("Fail")
+
+    try:
+        raise_my_exception_once()
+    except MyException:
+        pass
+
+.. testoutput::
+   :hide:
+
+   ...
+
 Retrying code block
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
